<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
                    xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib">

    <!-- {DynamicResource LOCMythos_} -->

    <!-- ================= Deliberate overrides of Playnite-global keys =================

         Everything after this block is theme-owned (LOCMythos_*) and safe to edit freely.
         These four are Playnite's own strings, so changing them changes Playnite's UI and
         not just the theme's. Each survived the HYP-166 audit on purpose; the rest were
         dropped. Do not add to this list without the same deliberation.

         The two blanks are U+2800 BRAILLE PATTERN BLANK - not whitespace, not a typo.
         Playnite will not take an empty string here, so a character that renders as nothing
         is how the notice gets suppressed. Confirmed intended 2026-08-20: the restart notice
         and the "* requires restart" marker are considered visually intrusive. The cost is
         real and accepted - somebody who installs an unrelated addon is no longer told a
         restart is needed. All 10 locales now carry the same blank, so the behaviour no
         longer depends on the user's language.

         LOCExitAppLabel / LOCOpenPlaynite are the Windows notification-area entries, i.e.
         outside the application entirely. Branded on purpose (HYP-200), reaffirmed 2026-08-20.

         LOCPlayGame is exposed as a ThemeModifier terminology setting (thememodifier.yaml,
         "Launch Button Label") and is the only override with a real theme consumer,
         DerivedStyles/PlayButton.xaml.

         Dropped by HYP-166, recorded so they are not reintroduced:
           LOCVersionLabel  was "Play Button" - it relabelled Playnite's *version* field,
                            had no theme consumer and was absent from thememodifier.yaml.
           LOCNotesLabel    was "Synopsis" - the theme's own Notes section renders no label,
                            so it only ever changed Playnite's own dialogs. -->
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCAddonChangesRestart">⠀</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCSettingsRestartNotification">⠀</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="LOCExitAppLabel">Exit VibeMythos</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCOpenPlaynite">Open VibeMythos</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="LOCPlayGame">Launch</sys:String>
